  "title": "Miscellaneous Aamaal for the Month of Rajab",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Sayyid Ibn Tawus has narrated that Muhammad ibn Zakwan - known as al-Sajjad due to his remarkable, time-consuming prostration during which he used to weep so heavily that he lost his sight - asked Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.), saying, “May Allah accept me as ransom for you! We are now in Rajab; I therefore please you to teach me a supplicatory prayer due to which Almighty Allah may help me.” Hence, the Imam (a.s.) asked him to write down the following:\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-Beneficent the All-Merciful. You may say the following (supplicatory prayer) each day in Rajab; in mornings, evenings, and after each of the obligatory prayers:\nيَا مَنْ اَرْجُوْهُ لِكُلِّ خَيْرٍ\nYAA MAN ARJOOHO LE KULLE KHAYRIN \nO He from whom I hope for every good,\nوَ آمَنُ سَخَطَهٗ عِنْدَ كُلِّ شَرٍّ\nWA AAMANO SAKHATAHU I’NDA KULLE SHARRIN \nAnd in whom I seek safety from His wrath at every evil.\nيَا مَنْ يُعْطِيْ الْكَثِيْرَ بِالْقَلِيْلِ\nYAA MAN YO’TIL KASEERAA BILQALEELE \nO He who gives much in return for very little (deeds),\nيَا مَنْ يُعْطِيْ مَنْ سَاَلَهٗ\nYAA MAN YO’TEE MAN SA-A’LAHU \nO He who gives to those who ask Him,\nيَا مَنْ يُعْطِيْ مَنْ لَمْ يَسْاَلْهٗ وَ مَنْ لَمْ يَعْرِفْهُ\nYAA MAN YO’TEE MAN LAM YAS-A’LHO WA MAN LAM YA’RIFHO\nO He who gives to those who do not ask Him and those who do not know Him,\nتَحَنُّنًا مِنْهُ وَ رَحْمَةً\nTAHANNONAN MINHO WA RAHMATAN \nOut of His affection and mercy.\nاَعْطِنِيْ بِمَسْاَلَتِيْ اِيَّاكَ\nAA’-TENEE BE-MASALATEE IYYAKA \nGrant me, by my asking of You, \nجَمِيْعَ خَيْرِ الدُّنْيَا وَ جَمِيْعَ خَيْرِ الْآخِرَةِ\nJAMEE-A’ KHAYRID DUNYAA WA JAMEE-A’ KHAYRIL AAKHERATE \nall the good of this world, and all the good of the Hereafter.\nوَ اصْرِفْ عَنِّيْ بِمَسْاَلَتِيْ اِيَّاكَ\nWAS RIF A’NNI BE MAS-ALATEE IYYAAKA \nAnd avert from me, by my asking of You,\nجَمِيْعَ شَرِّ الدُّنْيَا وَ شَرِّ الْآخِرَةِ\nJAMEE-A’ SHARRID DUNYAA WA SHARRIL AAKHERATE \nAll the evil of this world and the evil of the Hereafter.\nفَاِنَّهٗ غَيْرُ مَنْقُوْصٍ مَا اَعْطَيْتَ\nFA-INNAHU GHAYRO MANQOOSIN MA A-A’TAYTA \nFor indeed, whatever You give is never diminishing (from Your treasures),\nوَ زِدْنِي مِنْ فَضْلِكَ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nWA ZIDNEE MIN FAZLEKA YAA KAREEMO.\nAnd increase for me from Your bounty, O Most Generous.\nThe narrator then added that Imam al-Sadiq(a.s.) then grasped his beard with his left hand, while saying this supplicatory prayer, and moved ceaselessly the forefinger of his right hand. He then added:\nيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME \nO Possessor of Majesty and Honor,\nيَا ذَا النَّعْمَاءِ وَ الْجُوْدِ\nYAA ZAN NA’MAA-E WAL JOODE \nO Possessor of Blessings and Generosity,\nيَا ذَا الْمَنِّ وَ الطَّوْلِ\nYAA ZAL MANNE WAT TAWLE \nO Possessor of Favor and Bounty,\nحَرِّمْ شَيْبَتِيْ عَلَى النَّارِ\nHARRIM SHAYBATEE A’LAN NAAR.\nForbid my white beard (my aged self) from the Fire.\nNinth: The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is reported as saying: Whoever repeats the following imploration for forgiveness one hundred times in Rajab and immediately gives alms after it, Almighty Allah will conclude his life with mercy and forgiveness. Also, whoever repeats it four hundred times, will be given the reward of one hundred martyrs:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ الَّذِيْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHAL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA\nI implore the forgiveness of Allah. There is no god save Him,\nوَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nWAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU WA ATOOBO ELAYHE.\nI implore the forgiveness of Allah. There is no god save Him, and I repent before Him.\nTenth: The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is also reported to have said: Whoever repeats this litany one thousand times in Rajab, Almighty Allah will decide for him one hundred thousand rewards and award him one hundred houses in Paradise:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAH.\nThere is no god save Allah.\nEleventh: A Hadith reads that whoever repeats the following imploration for forgiveness seventy times in the morning and seventy times in the evening on each day in Rajab, will be admitted by Almighty Allah if he dies in Rajab and Hellfire will not touch him on account of the blessings of Rajab:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ وَ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHA WA ATOOBO ELAYHE.\nI implore the forgiveness of Allah and I repent to Him.\nAfter this imploration is repeated seventy times, it is recommended to raise the hands towards the sky and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيْ وَ تُبْ عَلَيَّ\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEE WA TUB A’LAYYA.\nO Allah, (please do) forgive me and accept my repentance.\nTwelfth: It is recommended to implore Almighty Allah for forgiveness in the following form one thousand times in Rajab so that He will forgive:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAH ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME\nI implore Allah, the Lord of majesty and honor,\nمِنْ جَمِيْعِ الذُّنُوْبِ وَ الْآثَامِ\nMIN JAMEE-I’Z ZONOOBE WAL AASAAME\nto forgive my all sins and offenses.\nThirteenth: In his book entitled Iqbal al-A’mal, Sayyid Ibn Tawus has mentioned great rewards for those who repeat [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) ten thousand, one thousand, or one hundred times in Rajab. Likewise, he has narrated that one who recites this Surah(of al-Tawheed) one hundred times on Fridays in Rajab will enjoy, on the Resurrection Day, light that draws him towards Paradise.\nFourteenth: Sayyid Ibn Tawus has also narrated that one who fasts on a day in Rajab and offers a four-unit prayer in the first unit of which he repeats Ayah al-Kursi one hundred times and in the second, [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) two hundred times, will not depart life before he sees (in sleep) his place in Paradise or someone else sees it on behalf of him.\nFifteenth: Sayyid Ibn Tawus has also reported from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that if one offer a four-unit prayer on Friday in Rajab between the obligatory Zohr and Asr Prayers in each unit of which [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once, Ayah al-Kursi repeated seven times, and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) five times; and then the following imploration for forgiveness repeated ten times - if one offers this prayer, Almighty Allah will decide for him since the day on which he offered this prayer and up to the day of his death one thousand rewards a day, a city built with ruby in Paradise for each verse (of the Holy Qur’an) he recites, a palace built with white pearls in Paradise for each letter he recites from the Holy Qur’an, Paradisiacal Women, ultimate pleasure, inclusion with the (true) worshippers, seal his life with happiness and forgiveness... etc. The supplicatory is as follows:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ الَّذِيْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ وَ اَسْاَلُهُ التَّوْبَةَ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHAL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA WA ASALOHUT TAWBAH.\nI seek forgiveness from Allah, there is no deity except Him, and I ask Him for repentance.\nSixteenth: It is recommended to fast on three days in the month of Rajab: Thursday, Friday, and Saturday. It has been narrated that whoever fasts on these three days in one of the Sacred Months will be awarded with the reward of nine hundred year worship.\nSeventeenth: It is recommended to offer a sixty-unit prayer in Rajab. Each night, it is recommended to offer two units of this prayer in the first unit of which [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once, [Surah al-Kafirun](A113) (No. 109) repeated three times, and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) recited one time. After the accomplishment of the two prayer units, it is recommended to raise the hands towards the sky and say the following:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU,\nThere is no god save Allah, the One and Only Who has no partner.\nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَ لَهُ الْحَمْدُ\nLAHUL MULKO WA LAHUL HAMDO, \nTo Him is the kingdom and to Him is all praise.\nيُحْيِيْ وَ يُمِيْتُ وَ هُوَ حَيٌّ لَا يَمُوْتُ\nYOHYEE WA YOMEETO WA HOWA HAYYUN LAA YAMOOTO \nHe restores to live and cause to die and He is Ever-living and He never dies.\nبِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ وَ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nBEYADEHIL KHAYRO WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAYIN QADEERUN \nIn His Hands is all goodness, He has power over all things,\nوَ اِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ\nWA ELAYHIL MASEERO, \nand to Him is the return of all things.\nوَ لَا حَوْلَ وَ لَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL A’ZEEME, \nThere is neither might nor strength save with Allah, the Most High, the All-great.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ النَّبِيِّ الْاُمِّيِّ وَ اٰلِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADENIN NABIYYIL UMMIYYE WA AALEHI.\nO Allah, (please do) bless Muhammad, the Ummi Prophet, and his Household.\nIt is also recommended to pass one’s hand over the face while uttering the last statement. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is reported to have said that if one offers this prayer and says this supplicatory prayer, Almighty Allah will respond to his needs and award him the reward of sixth times of Hajj and Umrah (ritual pilgrimage).\nEighteenth: It has been also narrated that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said, “One who recites [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) one hundred times at one night in Rajab will be decided to have fasted for one hundred years for the sake of Almighty Allah Who will also decide for him one hundred palaces (in Paradise) in the vicinity of one of the Prophets.”\nNineteenth: The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is also reported as saying that Almighty Allah will forgive all the sins of those who offer a ten unit prayer, at one night in Rajab, reciting in each unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and repeating [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) three times.\nTwentieth: In Zad al-Ma’ad, ‘Allamah al-Majlisi has mentioned that Imam Ali Ameer al-Momineen (a.s.) reported the following from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.): If one repeats the following Quranic chapters, litanies, and supplicatory prayers three times each day and each night in the months of Rajab, Sha’ban, and Ramadan, he will have all his sins forgiven even if they are as many as and as much as raindrops, tree leaves, sea foam... etc:\n(1) [Surah al-Faatehah](A5), (2) Ayah al-Kursi, (3) [Surah al-Kafirun](A113), (4) [Surah al-Tawheed](A116), (5) [Surah al-Falaq](A117), (6) [Surah al-Naas](A118), (7) the following litany:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHE, WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE \nAll glory be to Allah; all praise be to Allah;\nوَ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَ اللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nWA LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAL LAAHO AKBARO, \nthere is no god save Allah; Allah is the Greatest; \nوَ لَا حَوْلَ وَ لَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL A’ZEEM.\nand there is no might and no strength save with Allah, the High, the Magnificent.\n (8) the following invocation of blessings:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMDIN.\nO Allah bless Muhammad and his family\n (9) the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LIL MOAMENEENA WAL MOAMENAAT.\nAllah please forgive the believing men & women\n (10) the following imploration for forgiveness, yet four hundred times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ وَ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHA WA ATOOBO ELAYHE.\nI seek forgiveness from Allah, and I turn to Him in repentance.\n Allamah al-Majlisi has also mentioned that it is traditional to repeat the following litany one thousand times each night in Rajab:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAH.\nThere is no deity except Allah."
}
